<title>JAPAN: Markets should note strength of Japan economy - EPA.</title>
<headline>Markets should note strength of Japan economy - EPA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economic Planning Agency (EPA) Vice Minister Shimpei Nukaya said on Thursday that current economic conditions were fairly strong and he hoped the markets would take note of this.</p>
<p>Asked about the fall in stock prices and weakness in the yen's value against the dollar today, Nukaya told a news conference: &quot;I can't comment about the markets. I'm sure market participants are looking at various factors. But the current economic conditions are fairly strong and I hope that the markets would take note of this.&quot;</p>
</text>
